## What the review found

**Host truth correction.** The "0.1.2-alpha.2 host" label only describes the CLI/umbrella package. The global install's dependency closure is `0.1.2-rc.1` (cordis 4.0.4); a genuinely all-alpha.2 closure exists only in the pristine tree the pipeline downloaded (cordis 4.0.2). Both were booted for verification.

**Plane 1 — host settings/gateway** (`DSH-0.1.2-A1-08`, `A2-10`, API-01/03): the private `/bench-brand-text/api` `webServer` route bypassed the alpha.1+ bootstrap-token/signed-cookie gate and duplicated the official settings domain (`ctx.settings.installSection`, `settings.describe/update` via `ctx.settingsScope`). Retirement is the right call; but the registration body is elided, so the "web check pass" proves nothing, and the documented direct `installSection` call skips API-03's `ctx.inject(['settings'], …)` lifecycle.

**Plane 2 — browser slot/store half**: store-engine retarget to `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-store` is correct (baseline external, implicit) but comment-level only in the fixture (`DSH-0.1.2-A1-25`); context type moved to `@deepseek-ai/cordis` ✓; inject list recomposed and `settingsScope` added for strict injection ✓ (`DSH-0.1.1-R1-04`); peer cohort moved to alpha.2 with cordis `^4.0.1` ✓ (`A2-03`) — with residual gaps: **`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-renderer` (the `slots` service/declaration owner) is missing from peers and the type merge list**, exact peer pins don't satisfy the rc.1 closure, and the preferred `ctx.layout.setProductTitle` seam exists on **no released host** (fallback races `DocumentTitle`).

**Pre-existing / hygiene** (attributed, not charged to the migration): known-drifty 3-vs-4 effect test, `ui-brand-official` priority-0 single-slot collision, the `A1-26` bundle-id question, dangling `.dsh-migrate` pointers, and a new **npm-format `package-lock.json`** in a pnpm repo (untracked, unmentioned in any report).

**Deploy anchor — reproduced.** The pipeline only waited for the readiness line. I cold-booted an isolated profile twice (global alpha.2 with rc.1 closure, and the pristine alpha.2 binary), exchanged token→cookie, and read `globalThis.__DSH_BOOT__`: the client entry **`{"id":"@bench/dsh-bench-brand-text", …}`** is listed by package name (47 entries) and its advertised combo URL returns 200 (7792 bytes). Per `DSH-0.1.2-A1-19`/`A1-26`, the revision-less path 404s. Mount stays explicitly unproven: the served artifact contains zero `__ModuleLoader__.load` markers — the fixture's browser half is not a factory bundle.

